<template>
  <main class="report">
    <header class="masthead">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">AFFON / PERFORMANCE FACILITY</p><h1>Coverage report</h1><p class="subtitle">From declared workloads to measured performance gaps.</p></div>
      <div class="stamp"><span>{{ props.generated }}</span><strong>{{ props.target }}</strong></div>
    </header>

    <section class="notice"><strong>Current status</strong><span>Measured ratios are diagnostic. A linked result records a checked file; it does not establish model parity or release acceptance.</span></section>

    <section class="phases" aria-label="Performance work phases"><article #for="phase in props.phaseStatus"><span>{{ phase.name }}</span><strong>{{ phase.state }}</strong><p>{{ phase.detail }}</p></article></section>

    <section class="framework" aria-label="How the performance framework works">
      <div class="framework-head"><p class="eyebrow">READ THIS REPORT</p><h2>How the pieces fit</h2><p>A cell is one backend, dtype, operation, regime, and any declared dispatch variant. It represents work to classify and measure, not a completed test.</p></div>
      <div class="flow" aria-label="Main results flow">
        <article><span>1 · Declare</span><strong>{{ props.totalCells }} candidate cells</strong><p>Compute's operation and dtype list defines the planned cases. New execution variants get separate cells.</p></article>
        <article><span>2 · Check</span><strong>{{ props.probedCells }} correctness links</strong><p>Concrete shapes run against an independent output formula. Each check records the selected Affon path.</p></article>
        <article><span>3 · Measure</span><strong>{{ props.measuredCases }} operator comparisons</strong><p>Matched Affon and PyTorch runs produce raw timings. Selected cells also get multi operation Program runs.</p></article>
        <article><span>4 · Record checks</span><strong>{{ props.peerCells }} operator reports linked</strong><p>The checklist below counts recorded reports across all candidate cells.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-branch"><strong>Separate kernel choice checks · {{ props.boundaryChecks }} pairs</strong><span>{{ props.observedBoundaries }} selected a different implementation; {{ props.unobservedBoundaries }} selected the same one. These checks do not add operator timing results.</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="metrics">
      <article><span>Candidate cells</span><strong>{{ props.totalCells }}</strong><small>Across backend, dtype, operation, and regime</small></article>
      <article><span>Correctness linked</span><strong>{{ props.probedCells }}</strong><small>Independent output check and selected path</small></article>
      <article><span>Matched peer cells</span><strong>{{ props.peerCells }}</strong><small>Exact shape, output, and timing contract</small></article>
      <article><span>Still unknown</span><strong>{{ props.unknownCells }}</strong><small>Awaiting a recorded numerical check</small></article>
    </section>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">MATRIX DISTRIBUTION</p><h2>Where the candidate cells are</h2></div><p>{{ props.gpuCandidateCells }} GPU candidate cells = Metal + CUDA. The tables show declared cells and linked checks by backend, dtype, family, and backend × dtype. Candidates describe the test plan, not measured support.</p></section>
    <section class="distribution"><article #for="group in props.distribution"><h3>{{ group.dimension }}</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Candidates</th><th>Correctness linked</th><th>Operator peer linked</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr #for="item in group.rows"><td><strong>{{ item.name }}</strong></td><td>{{ item.candidate }}</td><td>{{ item.correctness_linked }}</td><td>{{ item.operator_peer_linked }}</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div></article></section>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / MEASURED CASES</p><h2>Operator comparison</h2></div><p>{{ props.measuredCases }} concrete cases from the candidate matrix have matched timing reports. Ratio = Affon median ÷ PyTorch median; above 1 is slower.</p></section>
    <div class="toolbar" aria-label="Operator filters"><input data-filter="query" type="search" placeholder="Search cell or path" :value="query" @input="updateQuery" /><label>Device <select data-filter="device" :value="device" @change="updateDevice"><option value="all">All devices</option><option #for="value in dimensions(props.cases, 0)" :value="value">{{ value }}</option></select></label><label>Operation <select data-filter="operation" :value="operation" @change="updateOperation"><option value="all">All operations</option><option #for="value in dimensions(props.cases, 2)" :value="value">{{ value }}</option></select></label><label>Dtype <select data-filter="dtype" :value="dtype" @change="updateDtype"><option value="all">All dtypes</option><option #for="value in dimensions(props.cases, 1)" :value="value">{{ value }}</option></select></label><label>Status <select data-filter="status" :value="status" @change="updateStatus"><option value="all">All statuses</option><option value="candidate_gap">Candidate gaps</option><option value="mixed_rounds">Mixed rounds</option><option value="within_diagnostic_target">Within diagnostic target</option></select></label></div><div class="pager" data-pager="operator"><span>{{ pageLabel(visibleCases().length, operatorPage) }}</span><button @click="previousOperator" :disabled="operatorPage === 0">Previous</button><button @click="nextOperator" :disabled="(operatorPage + 1) * pageSize >= visibleCases().length">Next</button></div>
    <div class="table-wrap operator-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th>Shape</th><th>Status</th><th>Affon total</th><th>PyTorch total</th><th>Affon execute / read</th><th>Ratio</th><th>Round ratios</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr #for="item in operatorPageCases()"><td><strong>{{ item.id }}</strong><small>{{ item.path }}</small></td><td>{{ item.shape }}</td><td><span :class="statusClass(item.status)">{{ statusLabel(item.status) }}</span></td><td>{{ formatMs(item.affon_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.peer_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatPhases(item.affon_execution_ms, item.affon_readback_ms) }}</td><td><strong>{{ formatRatio(item.ratio) }}</strong><div class="bar"><i :style="barStyle(item.ratio, item.status)"></i></div></td><td>{{ formatRounds(item.round_ratios) }}</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / MEASURED PROGRAMS</p><h2>Two operations together</h2></div><p>{{ props.programCases.length }} matched Program cases. Matmul uses the GPT-2 projection plus bias pattern; sum uses an explicitly synthetic composition. Inputs stay resident.</p></section>
    <div class="toolbar" aria-label="Program filters"><input data-filter="query" type="search" placeholder="Search cell or path" :value="programQuery" @input="updateProgramQuery" /><label>Device <select data-filter="device" :value="programDevice" @change="updateProgramDevice"><option value="all">All devices</option><option #for="value in dimensions(props.programCases, 0)" :value="value">{{ value }}</option></select></label><label>Operation <select data-filter="operation" :value="programOperation" @change="updateProgramOperation"><option value="all">All operations</option><option #for="value in dimensions(props.programCases, 2)" :value="value">{{ value }}</option></select></label><label>Dtype <select data-filter="dtype" :value="programDtype" @change="updateProgramDtype"><option value="all">All dtypes</option><option #for="value in dimensions(props.programCases, 1)" :value="value">{{ value }}</option></select></label><label>Status <select data-filter="status" :value="programStatus" @change="updateProgramStatus"><option value="all">All statuses</option><option value="candidate_gap">Candidate gaps</option><option value="mixed_rounds">Mixed rounds</option><option value="within_diagnostic_target">Within diagnostic target</option></select></label></div><div class="pager" data-pager="program"><span>{{ pageLabel(visiblePrograms().length, programPage) }}</span><button @click="previousProgram" :disabled="programPage === 0">Previous</button><button @click="nextProgram" :disabled="(programPage + 1) * pageSize >= visiblePrograms().length">Next</button></div><div class="table-wrap program-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th>Shape</th><th>Status</th><th>Affon total</th><th>PyTorch total</th><th>Affon execute / read</th><th>Ratio</th><th>Round ratios</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr #for="item in programPageCases()"><td><strong>{{ item.id }}</strong><small>{{ item.graph }}</small><small>{{ item.path }}</small></td><td>{{ item.shape }}</td><td><span :class="statusClass(item.status)">{{ statusLabel(item.status) }}</span></td><td>{{ formatMs(item.affon_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.peer_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatPhases(item.affon_execution_ms, item.affon_readback_ms) }}</td><td><strong>{{ formatRatio(item.ratio) }}</strong><div class="bar"><i :style="barStyle(item.ratio, item.status)"></i></div></td><td>{{ formatRounds(item.round_ratios) }}</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p class="section-note">These are diagnostic compositions that test Program execution overhead. They are not full model workloads. Their ratios can differ from the single operation table.</p>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / COVERAGE CHECKLIST</p><h2>What has been checked?</h2></div><p>For each of the {{ props.totalCells }} candidate cells, count which reports are linked. A linked report is a recorded check, not a speed verdict.</p></section>
    <section class="evidence"><article #for="item in props.evidence"><span>{{ item.label }}</span><strong>{{ item.linked }} of {{ props.totalCells }} cells</strong><p>{{ item.description }}</p><div class="track"><i :style="coverageStyle(item.linked)"></i></div><small>{{ item.missing }} cells still need this check</small></article></section>
    <p class="section-note">The four counts are separate checklists for the same candidate cells. The {{ props.measuredCases }} rows above come from operator timing reports; {{ props.peerCells }} operator reports are currently linked in this checklist.</p>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / BASELINE READINESS</p><h2>Are Affon timings repeatable?</h2></div><p>{{ props.baselineCalibrations.length }} calibration runs used fresh Affon processes. Baseline acceptance requires repeatability across independent sessions on a controlled target.</p></section>
    <p class="section-note">The provisional within-session screen marks a run stable if its medians differ by at most 1.10× or 0.05 ms. That screen alone cannot establish a baseline: independent sessions must agree under the same protocol and recorded target conditions. Accepted baseline cells: {{ props.acceptedBaselineCells }}.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Fresh runs</th><th>Run medians</th><th>Largest / smallest</th><th>Span</th><th>Baseline status</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr #for="item in props.baselineCalibrations"><td><strong>{{ item.id }}</strong></td><td>{{ item.protocol }}</td><td>{{ item.runs }}</td><td>{{ formatRunMedians(item.run_medians_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatRatio(item.spread_ratio) }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.spread_ms) }}</td><td>{{ item.status }}</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <h3 class="verdict-head">Independent session gate</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th>Session medians</th><th>Largest / smallest</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr #for="item in props.baselineVerdicts"><td><strong>{{ item.id }}</strong></td><td>{{ formatRunMedians(item.session_medians_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatRatio(item.ratio) }}</td><td>{{ baselineVerdictLabel(item.accepted) }}</td><td>{{ item.reasons }}</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <div class="gpu-note" #for="item in props.gpuProfiles"><strong>Drift between {{ item.sessions }} sessions · {{ item.id }}</strong><p>Session median GPU command times: {{ formatRunMedians(item.gpu_medians_ms) }} ({{ formatRatio(item.gpu_ratio) }} apart). Host operation totals: {{ formatRunMedians(item.host_medians_ms) }} ({{ formatRatio(item.host_ratio) }} apart). The same binary, protocol, and selected path produced both sessions. GPU command timing also drifted, so a separate GPU timing scope does not resolve baseline acceptance. These timestamps are diagnostic; profiling callbacks affect host totals.</p></div>
    <section #if="props.gpuInvestigationRuns.length > 0"><h3 class="verdict-head">Focused GPU timing investigation</h3>
      <p class="section-note">GPU command and host timing by fresh process. Power and thermal snapshots accompany the retained JSON; these coarse readings do not identify a cause for timing changes.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Session</th><th>Process</th><th>GPU command median</th><th>Host operation median</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr #for="item in props.gpuInvestigationRuns"><td>{{ item.session }}</td><td>{{ item.run }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.gpu_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.host_ms) }}</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div></section>
    <section #if="props.pairedGpuSessions.length > 0"><h3 class="verdict-head">Alternating cell check</h3>
      <p class="section-note">Adjacent sessions compare two cells under matching measurement identities. GPU session spread by cell: <span #for="change in props.pairedGpuChanges">{{ change.cell_id }} {{ formatRatio(change.gpu_session_ratio) }}. </span>This diagnostic alone cannot identify the cause of timing changes.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Pair</th><th>Cell</th><th>GPU command median</th><th>Host operation median</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr #for="item in props.pairedGpuSessions"><td>{{ item.pair }}</td><td>{{ item.cell_id }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.gpu_median_ms) }}</td><td>{{ formatMs(item.host_median_ms) }}</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div></section>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / KERNEL CHOICE CHECKS</p><h2>When does Affon switch implementations?</h2></div><p>Change one input near a dispatch rule, check both answers, and compare the selected implementation. These are {{ props.boundaryChecks }} pairs of checks, separate from timing measurements.</p></section>
    <p class="section-note">For matmul, shape is M × K × N, or batch × M × K × N. “Dense input hint” is the compile option supplied to Affon. “Same implementation” leaves the expected path change unobserved.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap boundary-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule being checked</th><th>One side: shape · implementation</th><th>Other side: shape · implementation</th><th>What happened?</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr #for="boundary in props.boundaries"><td><strong>{{ boundary.predicate }}</strong><small>{{ boundary.id }}</small></td><td><strong>{{ boundary.below_shape }}</strong><small>{{ boundary.below_hint }}</small><small>{{ boundary.below }}</small></td><td><strong>{{ boundary.at_shape }}</strong><small>{{ boundary.at_hint }}</small><small>{{ boundary.at }}</small></td><td>{{ boundaryLabel(boundary.status) }}</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>

    <section class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">06 / NEXT ACTION</p><h2>What the data says</h2></div></section>
    <section class="insights"><article #for="insight in props.insights"><strong>{{ insight.title }}</strong><p>{{ insight.body }}</p></article></section>
    <footer>Generated from retained JSON artifacts · Affon performance facility · {{ props.generated }}</footer>
  </main>
</template>

<script lang="ts">
  export interface CaseRow { id: string; status: string; shape: string; affon_ms: number; peer_ms: number; affon_execution_ms?: number; affon_readback_ms?: number; ratio: number; round_ratios: number[]; path: string; graph?: string }
  export interface EvidenceRow { label: string; description: string; linked: number; missing: number }
  export interface Insight { title: string; body: string }
  export interface Boundary { id: string; status: string; predicate: string; below: string; at: string; below_shape: string; at_shape: string; below_hint: string; at_hint: string }
  export interface BaselineCalibration { id: string; status: string; runs: number; protocol: string; run_medians_ms: number[]; spread_ratio: number; spread_ms: number }
  export interface BaselineVerdict { id: string; accepted: boolean; session_medians_ms: number[]; ratio: number; reasons: string }
  export interface GpuProfile { id: string; sessions: number; gpu_medians_ms: number[]; host_medians_ms: number[]; gpu_ratio: number; host_ratio: number }
  export interface GpuInvestigationRun { session: number; run: number; gpu_ms: number; host_ms: number; power: string; thermal: string }
  export interface PairedGpuSession { pair: number; cell_id: string; gpu_median_ms: number; host_median_ms: number }
  export interface PairedGpuChange { cell_id: string; gpu_session_ratio: number }
  export interface PhaseStatus { name: string; state: string; detail: string }
  export interface DistributionRow { name: string; candidate: number; supported: number; correctness_linked: number; operator_peer_linked: number }
  export interface DistributionGroup { dimension: string; rows: DistributionRow[] }
  export interface Props { generated: string; target: string; totalCells: number; gpuCandidateCells: number; probedCells: number; peerCells: number; acceptedBaselineCells: number; unknownCells: number; measuredCases: number; boundaryChecks: number; observedBoundaries: number; unobservedBoundaries: number; cases: CaseRow[]; programCases: CaseRow[]; baselineCalibrations: BaselineCalibration[]; baselineVerdicts: BaselineVerdict[]; gpuProfiles: GpuProfile[]; gpuInvestigationRuns: GpuInvestigationRun[]; pairedGpuSessions: PairedGpuSession[]; pairedGpuChanges: PairedGpuChange[]; phaseStatus: PhaseStatus[]; distribution: DistributionGroup[]; evidence: EvidenceRow[]; insights: Insight[]; boundaries: Boundary[] }
  export let props: Props;
  const pageSize = 100;
  let query = "", device = "all", operation = "all", dtype = "all", status = "all", operatorPage = 0;
  let programQuery = "", programDevice = "all", programOperation = "all", programDtype = "all", programStatus = "all", programPage = 0;
  function dimensions(rows: CaseRow[], position: number) { const seen: Record<string, boolean> = {}; const result: string[] = []; for (let index = 0; index < rows.length; index++) { const value = rows[index].id.split("/")[position]; if (value && !seen[value]) { seen[value] = true; result.push(value); } } return result.sort(); }
  function filterRows(rows: CaseRow[], search: string, backend: string, op: string, kind: string, state: string) { const result: CaseRow[] = []; for (let index = 0; index < rows.length; index++) { const item = rows[index], parts = item.id.split("/"); if ((backend === "all" || parts[0] === backend) && (op === "all" || parts[2] === op) && (kind === "all" || parts[1] === kind) && (state === "all" || item.status === state) && (!search || item.id.toLowerCase().includes(search) || item.path.toLowerCase().includes(search) || (item.graph || "").toLowerCase().includes(search))) result.push(item); } return result; }
  function visibleCases() { return filterRows(props.cases, query, device, operation, dtype, status); }
  function visiblePrograms() { return filterRows(props.programCases, programQuery, programDevice, programOperation, programDtype, programStatus); }
  function operatorPageCases() { return visibleCases().slice(operatorPage * pageSize, (operatorPage + 1) * pageSize); }
  function programPageCases() { return visiblePrograms().slice(programPage * pageSize, (programPage + 1) * pageSize); }
  function pageLabel(count: number, page: number) { return count ? `${page * pageSize + 1}–${Math.min((page + 1) * pageSize, count)} of ${count} matches` : "0 matches"; }
  function updateQuery(event: Event) { query = (event.target as HTMLInputElement).value.toLowerCase().trim(); operatorPage = 0; }
  function updateDevice(event: Event) { device = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; operatorPage = 0; }
  function updateOperation(event: Event) { operation = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; operatorPage = 0; }
  function updateDtype(event: Event) { dtype = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; operatorPage = 0; }
  function updateStatus(event: Event) { status = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; operatorPage = 0; }
  function updateProgramQuery(event: Event) { programQuery = (event.target as HTMLInputElement).value.toLowerCase().trim(); programPage = 0; }
  function updateProgramDevice(event: Event) { programDevice = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; programPage = 0; }
  function updateProgramOperation(event: Event) { programOperation = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; programPage = 0; }
  function updateProgramDtype(event: Event) { programDtype = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; programPage = 0; }
  function updateProgramStatus(event: Event) { programStatus = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; programPage = 0; }
  function previousOperator() { if (operatorPage > 0) operatorPage--; }
  function nextOperator() { if ((operatorPage + 1) * pageSize < visibleCases().length) operatorPage++; }
  function previousProgram() { if (programPage > 0) programPage--; }
  function nextProgram() { if ((programPage + 1) * pageSize < visiblePrograms().length) programPage++; }
  function statusLabel(value: string) { return value === "candidate_gap" ? "Candidate gap" : value === "mixed_rounds" ? "Mixed rounds" : "Within target"; }
  function statusClass(value: string) { return "pill " + (value === "candidate_gap" ? "gap" : value === "mixed_rounds" ? "mixed" : "within"); }
  function boundaryLabel(value: string) { return value === "expected_transition" ? "Different implementation selected" : value === "unobserved_transition" ? "Same implementation selected · open" : "Check failed · investigate"; }
  function baselineVerdictLabel(accepted: boolean) { return accepted ? "Eligible for review" : "Rejected"; }
  function formatMs(value: number) { return (value * 1000).toFixed(1) + " µs"; }
  function formatPhases(execute?: number, read?: number) { return execute === undefined || read === undefined ? "—" : formatMs(execute) + " / " + formatMs(read); }
  function formatRatio(value: number) { return value.toFixed(2) + "×"; }
  function formatRounds(values: number[]) { const parts: string[] = []; for (let index = 0; index < values.length; index++) parts.push(values[index].toFixed(2) + "×"); return parts.join(" / "); }
  function formatRunMedians(values: number[]) { const parts: string[] = []; for (let index = 0; index < values.length; index++) parts.push(formatMs(values[index])); return parts.join(" / "); }
  function barStyle(value: number, state: string) { return "width:" + Math.min(100, value / 8 * 100) + "%;background:" + (state === "candidate_gap" ? "#d46c4c" : state === "mixed_rounds" ? "#d9ad55" : "#5b9b89"); }
  function coverageStyle(value: number) { return "width:" + (value / props.totalCells * 100) + "%"; }
</script>

<style>
  .distribution{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.distribution article:nth-child(n+3){grid-column:1/-1}.distribution h3{text-transform:capitalize;font-size:15px;margin:0 0 10px;color:#234a43}.distribution td:first-child{min-width:120px}.distribution td{padding:10px 14px}@media(max-width:850px){.distribution{grid-template-columns:1fr}.distribution article:nth-child(n+3){grid-column:auto}}
  .phases{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin:0 0 28px}.phases article{padding:18px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce6dc;border-radius:11px}.phases span{display:block;color:#39756e;font-size:12px;font-weight:800}.phases strong{display:block;margin:8px 0;font-size:16px}.phases p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#65776e;margin:0}@media(max-width:700px){.phases{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  .gpu-note{background:#eaf1ee;border-left:3px solid #5b9b89;padding:17px 20px;margin-top:14px;border-radius:0 9px 9px 0}.gpu-note strong{font-size:13px;color:#234a43}.gpu-note p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#526a61;margin:7px 0 0}
  .verdict-head{font-size:15px;margin:25px 0 12px;color:#234a43}
  .section-note{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#64736e;margin:13px 0 16px;max-width:1000px}.evidence article p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#64736e;margin:0}.boundary-table td:nth-child(2) small,.boundary-table td:nth-child(3) small{display:block;color:#7a8983;margin-top:5px}.boundary-table td:nth-child(2) strong,.boundary-table td:nth-child(3) strong{display:block;color:#29433d}
  .framework{margin:28px 0 35px;padding:25px;border:1px solid #cddcd4;border-radius:16px;background:#edf3ec}.framework-head h2{font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:0 0 8px}.framework-head p:last-child{font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#526a61;max-width:800px;margin:0 0 20px}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px}.flow article{position:relative;padding:18px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce6dc;border-radius:11px}.flow article:not(:last-child):after{content:"→";position:absolute;right:-13px;top:35px;z-index:1;color:#39756e;font-size:20px;font-weight:700}.flow span{display:block;color:#39756e;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.flow strong{display:block;margin:9px 0;font-size:17px;letter-spacing:-.02em}.flow p{margin:0;color:#65776e;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55}.boundary-branch{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:baseline;border-top:1px solid #d2dfd3;margin-top:18px;padding-top:16px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}.boundary-branch strong{white-space:nowrap;color:#234a43}.boundary-branch span{color:#526a61}@media(max-width:1000px){.flow{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.flow article:after{display:none}}@media(max-width:600px){.flow{grid-template-columns:1fr}.boundary-branch{display:block}.boundary-branch span{display:block;margin-top:6px}.framework{padding:18px}}
  :global(*){box-sizing:border-box} :global(body){margin:0;background:#f6f5f0;color:#1b2a2a;font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif} :global(button),:global(input),:global(select){font:inherit}
  .report{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:44px 42px 26px}.masthead{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:24px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8ded7;padding-bottom:33px}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#39756e;margin:0 0 12px}.masthead h1{font-size:clamp(36px,4vw,56px);line-height:1;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.055em}.subtitle{color:#62716f;margin:15px 0 0;font-size:15px}.stamp{text-align:right;display:grid;gap:7px;color:#687875;font-size:12px}.stamp strong{font-size:13px;color:#213a37}.notice{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:center;background:#e8eee8;border-left:3px solid #39756e;padding:15px 18px;margin:30px 0;color:#49615c;font-size:13px}.notice strong{color:#234a43;white-space:nowrap}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px}.metrics article,.evidence article,.insights article{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e1e6df;border-radius:14px;padding:20px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px #203e3010}.metrics article{display:grid;gap:8px}.metrics span,.evidence span{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:#63736e}.metrics strong{font-size:33px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.04em}.metrics small,.evidence small{font-size:11px;color:#83908b}.section-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:24px;margin:52px 0 17px}.section-head h2{font-size:25px;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:0}.section-head p:last-child{font-size:12px;color:#78857f;max-width:420px;margin:0 0 4px}.toolbar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:12px}.toolbar input,.toolbar select{border:1px solid #d6ddd5;background:white;border-radius:8px;padding:11px 13px;color:#28403b}.toolbar input{flex:1;min-width:170px}.toolbar label{display:grid;gap:4px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#526a61}.toolbar select{min-width:120px}.pager{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:0 0 12px;color:#526a61;font-size:12px}.pager span{margin-right:8px}.pager button{border:1px solid #d6ddd5;background:white;border-radius:7px;padding:7px 11px;color:#28403b;cursor:pointer}.pager button:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:default}.table-wrap{border:1px solid #e1e6df;border-radius:13px;overflow:auto;background:white}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px}th{text-align:left;background:#f1f4ef;color:#697971;font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;padding:15px 16px;white-space:nowrap}td{border-top:1px solid #edf0eb;padding:15px 16px;vertical-align:middle;white-space:nowrap}td:first-child{min-width:295px}td:first-child strong{display:block;color:#203d37}td:first-child small{display:block;color:#86918c;margin-top:4px}td:last-child{color:#7a8983}.pill{display:inline-block;padding:6px 9px;border-radius:20px;font-size:10px;font-weight:800}.gap{background:#fae9e3;color:#a84f34}.mixed{background:#fbf2dd;color:#99742c}.within{background:#e7f1ea;color:#377563}.bar,.track{height:5px;background:#edf1eb;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:8px;min-width:70px}.bar i,.track i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:8px}.evidence{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px}.evidence article{display:grid;gap:11px}.evidence strong{font-size:23px;letter-spacing:-.04em}.track{margin:0}.track i{background:#4e9b85;min-width:2px}.insights{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px}.insights article strong{font-size:13px}.insights article p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.65;color:#64736e;margin:10px 0 0}footer{border-top:1px solid #d8ded7;margin-top:55px;padding-top:16px;color:#89958e;font-size:11px}@media(max-width:850px){.report{padding:27px 17px}.metrics,.evidence{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.insights{grid-template-columns:1fr}.stamp{display:none}.section-head{display:block}.section-head p:last-child{margin-top:9px}.toolbar{flex-wrap:wrap}.toolbar input{width:100%;flex:auto}}@media(max-width:500px){.metrics,.evidence{grid-template-columns:1fr}.notice{display:block}.notice span{display:block;margin-top:7px}}
</style>
